# Monorepo and deploy

## Package boundaries

| Package | May depend on |
|---------|----------------|
| `packages/contract` | Zod, oRPC contract only |
| `packages/client` | `contract` |
| `packages/db` | Prisma only (no Nest, no Expo) |
| `packages/brand` | nothing app-specific |
| `apps/api` | `contract`, `db`, Nest |
| `apps/mobile` | `client`, `contract`, `brand` |
| `apps/web` | `client`/`contract` as needed, `brand` |
| `apps/admin` | `client`, `contract`, `brand`, Next.js |

Apps must not import each other’s `src`. Shared code goes in `packages/*`.

## Workspace protocol

Internal deps use `workspace:*`. Do not publish private packages unless splitting repos.

## Deploy portability

- One API Docker image for Render and AWS.
- Bind `0.0.0.0`, honor `PORT`.
- Separate liveness vs readiness (DB on readiness only).
- Migrations via pre-deploy (`prisma migrate deploy`), never on process boot.
- No AWS/Render SDK types inside domain/services.

## Tooling

Node/pnpm via `.mise.toml`. Root scripts orchestrate; package scripts own the work.
`Makefile` targets must echo the underlying command.
